    "Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)"
  ],
  "Tags": [
    "Features"
  ],
  "Body": {
    "ContentType": "html",
    "Content": "<p>We are extending&nbsp;<a href=\"https://nam06.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.microsoft.com%2Fen-us%2Fazure%2Faks%2Fuse-network-policies&amp;data=05%7C01%7Ckparekh%40microsoft.com%7C5ce99d45e43245066f9c08da820aa047%7C72f988bf86f141af91ab2d7cd011db47%7C1%7C0%7C637965279401308614%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=Bm5IPRMzdrksjdAzY%2BZOi281nO1QwVZyo7SsAoKLrhs%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Azure Network Policy Manager (NPM)</a> to Windows server 2022 for AKS.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Security rules from&nbsp;<a href=\"https://nam06.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fkubernetes.io%2Fdocs%2Fconcepts%2Fservices-networking%2Fnetwork-policies%2F&amp;data=05%7C01%7Ckparekh%40microsoft.com%7C5ce99d45e43245066f9c08da820aa047%7C72f988bf86f141af91ab2d7cd011db47%7C1%7C0%7C637965279401308614%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=jSKcJ%2B2Ek72ziO20%2BjP8ViSHHIMKb4xF6c0G2STcKP0%3D&amp;reserved=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Kubernetes Network Policy resources</a> can now be enforced on all pod traffic across Linux and Windows Server 2022 nodes, for a cluster created with&nbsp;--network-policy=azure.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Network Policy Manager&nbsp;continues to be a managed solution, configurable at cluster creation.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/aks/use-network-policies\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Learn more</a>.</p>\r\n",
    "Markdown": "We are extending Azure Network Policy Manager (NPM) to Windows server 2022 for AKS.\n\nSecurity rules from Kubernetes Network Policy resources can now be enforced on all pod traffic across Linux and Windows Server 2022 nodes, for a cluster created with --network-policy=azure.\n\nNetwork Policy Manager continues to be a managed solution, configurable at cluster creation.\n\nLearn more ."
  },
